 R←Test_Stash_014(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;dir;rc;msg;buff;vec
⍝ Executes StashListContent with "noAPLnames" in ⍺. The result is then a VECTOR of filenames
⍝ rather than the two-column matrix the default returns - the shape ]StashListContent promises
⍝ with -noAPLnames. Neither the shape nor the left argument itself was covered here.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 dir←∆StashDir,'/SourceCode'
 'Create!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath dir

 (⊂'Hello')⎕NPUT(dir,'/file_3.txt')1
 ∆StashDir ##.APLGit2.Add''
 buff←##.APLGit2.StashPush ∆StashDir
 Assert∨/'Saved working directory and index state WIP on main'⍷∊buff

 buff←##.APLGit2.StashListContent ∆StashDir 0        ⍝ The default: a two-column matrix
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠⍴⍴buff
 vec←1 ##.APLGit2.StashListContent ∆StashDir 0       ⍝ With the flag: the filenames alone
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠⍴⍴vec
 →T.GoToTidyUp vec≢,buff[;1]

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ##.APLGit2.StashClear ∆StashDir
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce dir
 msg Assert 0=rc
⍝Done
